              "label": "Submit",
              "type": "button",
              "mode": "business_logic",
              "handler": "system",
              "validate_and_save": true,
              "business_logic": {
                "method": "submit_expense_and_create_report",
                "description": "Create and submit the expense as a new report for Management Approval",
                "spec": "When Submit is invoked and this expense row's EXPENSE_REPORT column is blank/NULL: (1) auto-generate a new REPORT_ID using the same auto_generate() convention used elsewhere in this project (e.g. RPT-00001 style, unique). (2) INSERT one row into EXPTRACK_EXPENSE_REPORT with values read LIVE from this expense row (never hard-coded or sample values): REPORT_ID = the new id; REPORT_TITLE = this expense's TRIP_NAME (the trip name auto-filled on the expense from EXPTRACK_TRIP.TRIP_NAME via the TRIP lookup, e.g. 'Client Lucknow'); EMPLOYEE = this expense's EMPLOYEE; REPORT_DATE = today(); TOTAL_AMOUNT = this expense's AMOUNT; STATUS = \"Submitted\"; TRIP = this expense's TRIP; CATEGORY_NAME = the CATEGORY_NAME looked up from EXPTRACK_EXPENSE_CATEGORY where CATEGORY_CODE = this expense's CATEGORY; PAYMENT_METHOD_NAME = the PAYMENT_METHOD_NAME looked up from EXPTRACK_PAYMENT_METHOD where PAYMENT_METHOD_CODE = this expense's PAYMENT_METHOD; CURRENCY = this expense's CURRENCY; RECEIPT_ATTACHMENT = this expense's RECEIPT_ATTACHMENT; DESCRIPTION = this expense's DESCRIPTION. (3) UPDATE EXPTRACK_EXPENSE SET EXPENSE_REPORT = the new REPORT_ID, STATUS = \"Submitted\" WHERE EXPENSE_ID = this expense's EXPENSE_ID. If EXPENSE_REPORT is already populated (resubmission case), skip steps 1-2 but still re-sync every mirrored field on the existing EXPTRACK_EXPENSE_REPORT row (REPORT_TITLE, EMPLOYEE, TOTAL_AMOUNT, CURRENCY, CATEGORY_NAME, PAYMENT_METHOD_NAME, RECEIPT_ATTACHMENT, DESCRIPTION) from this expense's CURRENT values before setting STATUS = \"Submitted\" on both rows, so the two records can never drift apart. No field on the report row may ever be left as a static/sample/placeholder value. Return a confirmation message such as \"Expense <EXPENSE_ID> submitted; Report <REPORT_ID> created for approval.\""
              },
              "visible_when": "{form.status} == \"Draft\" or {form.status} == \"Added-to-Report\"",
              "validations": [
                {
                  "type": "expression",
                  "name": "Expense must be in Draft or Added-to-Report status",
                  "error_code": "EXP_NOT_DRAFT",
                  "message": "This expense cannot be submitted because it is not in Draft or Added-to-Report status.",
                  "expression": "{form.status} == \"Draft\" or {form.status} == \"Added-to-Report\"",
                  "disabled": true
                }
              ],
              "order": 1,
              "system_op": "save"
            }
          ],
          "validations": [
            {
              "type": "business_logic",
              "name": "Log expense activity",
              "business_logic": {
                "method": "log_expense_activity",
                "description": "Write an Activity Log entry for add/update/delete of an expense",
                "spec": "On add/edit/delete of an EXPTRACK_EXPENSE row, insert an Activity Log entry capturing the actor (logged-in user), the action performed (Added/Updated/Deleted), the expense_id, and a narrative description (e.g. 'John Doe added Expense EXP-1023'). Use payload's _action ('add'/'edit') to determine wording; this validation never blocks the save (always return null/None on success), it only records the log entry as a side effect."
              }
            }
          ]
        }
      }
    ],
