        "spec": "Fire after save of an EXPTRACK_EXPENSE row whenever this Submit produced STATUS = 'Submitted' (i.e. runs as part of the same Submit action that already sets EXPTRACK_EXPENSE.STATUS to 'Submitted' and creates/links the EXPTRACK_EXPENSE_REPORT row). If no row exists yet in EXPTRACK_MANAGE_APPROVAL_NEW_TXN where EXPENSE_ID = this expense's EXPENSE_ID: auto-generate a new APPROVAL_ID (auto_generate() convention) and INSERT one row into EXPTRACK_MANAGE_APPROVAL_NEW_TXN reading LIVE values from this just-saved expense row: EXPENSE_ID = this expense's EXPENSE_ID; EMPLOYEE = this expense's EMPLOYEE; TRIP = this expense's TRIP; CATEGORY = this expense's CATEGORY; EXPENSE_DATE = this expense's EXPENSE_DATE; AMOUNT = this expense's AMOUNT; PAYMENT_METHOD = this expense's PAYMENT_METHOD; STATUS = 'Pending'; APPROVER_NAME = this expense's APPROVER column value (EXPTRACK_EXPENSE.APPROVER). If a Manage Approval row already exists for this EXPENSE_ID (resubmission case), do not insert a duplicate \u2014 instead re-sync EMPLOYEE, TRIP, CATEGORY, EXPENSE_DATE, AMOUNT, PAYMENT_METHOD and APPROVER_NAME on the existing row from this expense's current values, leaving its STATUS untouched. No field may ever be left as a static/sample/placeholder value."
      }
